   128:- compensation: pay a party for a loss caused by the other party or the platform (may exceed the disputed charge, up to ${disputedAmount(record) * COMPENSATION_CAP_MULTIPLIER} ${currency(record)})
   129:- no_action: the charge stands (e.g. a no-show fee is upheld and stays with the driver); amount 0,
   130:  recipient "none". Use no_action when the ruling is inconclusive.
   131:Refunds (full_refund, partial_refund) can never exceed the disputed charge (${disputedAmount(record)} ${currency(record)}). Show the calculation in basis.
   132:partyNotices are short messages (3-5 sentences) sent to each party: plain, respectful language
   133:addressed to that person ("you"), stating the outcome, any amount and when it applies, the main
   134:reason in everyday terms, and that they can reply to appeal. No JSON paths, internal agent names or
   135:confidence scores, and nothing about the other party beyond what the decision needs.
